      "name": "Scrooge's Counting-House",
      "description": "It is Christmas Eve and the fog pours in at every chink and keyhole of Scrooge's counting-house. Scrooge keeps the coal-box by his own very small fire, while beyond the open door, in a dismal little cell like a tank, the clerk copies letters by a fire no bigger than one coal. The city clocks have only just gone three but it is quite dark already, and candles flare in the neighbouring offices like ruddy smears upon the brown air. The door east leads up the dark yard to Scrooge's chambers.",
