    {
      "id": "scrooge-chambers",
      "name": "Scrooge's Chambers",
      "description": "A gloomy suite of rooms up a dark yard, once Jacob Marley's and now Scrooge's: sitting-room, bedroom and lumber-room. A very low fire burns in a grate paved all round with quaint Dutch tiles, a saucepan of gruel waits on the hob, and a disused bell hangs silent on the wall. The dressing-gown hangs in a suspicious attitude against the wall, and from the cellar below comes now and then a clanking, as of chains dragged over casks. West is the way back to the counting-house, north a door opens on the warehouse of long ago, and east lies Camden Town and the Cratchits' house.",
