    {
      "id": "fezziwig-warehouse",
      "name": "Fezziwig's Warehouse",
      "description": "Old Fezziwig's warehouse on Christmas Eve, the shutters up and every movable packed off, the floor swept and watered, the lamps trimmed and fuel heaped upon the fire. Fezziwig's high desk stands at one end, ready for the fiddler to make an orchestra of it, and along the wall wait cake, negus, cold roast, cold boiled, mince-pies and plenty of beer. The warehouse is as snug and warm and dry and bright a ball-room as you would desire to see upon a winter's night, with room for twenty couple at once. The only door is south, back to Scrooge's chambers.",
